{
  "case_id": "2006-05-785",
  "document_hash": "4c248d0c5593e03babd6a9a038208dbf64ae4cbfd9243e184c96d2d1537477a1",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2006-05-785",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4c248d0c5593e03babd6a9a038208dbf64ae4cbfd9243e184c96d2d1537477a1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4c248d0c5593-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 11:03 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (Gregory A. Ott)",
      "case_id": "2006-05-785",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4c248d0c5593e03babd6a9a038208dbf64ae4cbfd9243e184c96d2d1537477a1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4c248d0c5593-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Mr. OTT: Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: This Court has never addressed the constitutionality of photo buttons worn by spectators during a criminal trial. The two closest decisions of this Court, Estelle v. Williams and Holbrook v. Flynn established only a general rule that some courtroom practices may be so inherently prejudicial that they violate the defendant's right to a fair trial."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2006-05-785",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4c248d0c5593e03babd6a9a038208dbf64ae4cbfd9243e184c96d2d1537477a1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4c248d0c5593-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOUTER: Well, it went a little bit beyond that. I mean, the -- Justice Marshall announced not merely the possibility of inherent prejudice, but he spoke in terms of practices that raised a risk that improper factors would come into play in the jury decision. Isn't that the criterion?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (Gregory A. Ott)",
      "case_id": "2006-05-785",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4c248d0c5593e03babd6a9a038208dbf64ae4cbfd9243e184c96d2d1537477a1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4c248d0c5593-0000-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Below, however, on Federal habeas review, the circuit court of appeals used its own circuit case to define clearly established law under AEDPA. Instead of assessing the state court's application of the general rule, the circuit court narrowed this Court's general rule into one that specifically condemned buttons."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2006-05-785",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4c248d0c5593e03babd6a9a038208dbf64ae4cbfd9243e184c96d2d1537477a1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4c248d0c5593-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 10,
        "start": 10
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: Suppose all of the -- suppose there are five circuits. They're the only ones that looked at the issue. And they all say, we think the general rule of the Supreme Court is as follows, isn't that entitled to some weight?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2006-05-785",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4c248d0c5593e03babd6a9a038208dbf64ae4cbfd9243e184c96d2d1537477a1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4c248d0c5593-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, what's wrong with that? The prosecutor is going to get up and urge the jury to convict him. What is wrong with it on the button? What risk does the button raise that the prosecutor's argument does not?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2006-05-785",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4c248d0c5593e03babd6a9a038208dbf64ae4cbfd9243e184c96d2d1537477a1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4c248d0c5593-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "How different is it from the victim's family sitting in the second row behind the prosecution every day of the trial?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2006-05-785",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4c248d0c5593e03babd6a9a038208dbf64ae4cbfd9243e184c96d2d1537477a1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4c248d0c5593-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What about simply the facts that we have in this case, which I thought I was doing, maybe I wasn't clear about it, but the button is different. Instead of putting a picture of the victim, it's got the statement, \"Hang Musladin.\" It's worn every day by three members of his family who sit behind the prosecution table within the sight of the jury. Assume those facts. Would habeas relief be required under the general rule?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2006-05-785",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4c248d0c5593e03babd6a9a038208dbf64ae4cbfd9243e184c96d2d1537477a1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4c248d0c5593-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Required? Should -- look, should a court grant habeas relief on my facts?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Ott",
      "case_id": "2006-05-785",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4c248d0c5593e03babd6a9a038208dbf64ae4cbfd9243e184c96d2d1537477a1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4c248d0c5593-0001-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, as Mr. Chief Justice pointed out, three family members of the victim sitting in the front row, buttons or not, the buttons don't add -- add little, if anything, to the three victim's family members sitting there grieving through a trial. They add very little, for instance, in this case --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2006-05-785",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4c248d0c5593e03babd6a9a038208dbf64ae4cbfd9243e184c96d2d1537477a1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4c248d0c5593-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Okay, assuming that explicit message, could habeas relief be granted in my hypothetical case?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Fermino",
      "case_id": "2006-05-785",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4c248d0c5593e03babd6a9a038208dbf64ae4cbfd9243e184c96d2d1537477a1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4c248d0c5593-0001-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I want to direct this Court's attention to the state court opinion which appears at 55A to 78A of the appendix to the petition for writ of certiorari in this case. I want Your Honors to take a look at that opinion. It is 25 pages in length, but the portion of the opinion dealing with the buttons issue is two pages in length."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2006-05-785",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4c248d0c5593e03babd6a9a038208dbf64ae4cbfd9243e184c96d2d1537477a1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4c248d0c5593-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: But there have been -- haven't there been court decisions that have held that buttons didn't compromise a fair trial right?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2006-05-785",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4c248d0c5593e03babd6a9a038208dbf64ae4cbfd9243e184c96d2d1537477a1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4c248d0c5593-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: The record is confusing, at least as I read it -- please correct me if I'm wrong -- on the showing of how many days these buttons were worn. A, is it clear from the record how many days the buttons were worn?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2006-05-785",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4c248d0c5593e03babd6a9a038208dbf64ae4cbfd9243e184c96d2d1537477a1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4c248d0c5593-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Where does it say in there that the buttons were worn every day?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (Mr. Fermino)",
      "case_id": "2006-05-785",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4c248d0c5593e03babd6a9a038208dbf64ae4cbfd9243e184c96d2d1537477a1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4c248d0c5593-0002-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 43,
        "start": 43
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. FERMINO: I think in looking at the rule again derived from Williams and Flynn, we don't have to go there. It's the risk, not the reality. I don't know what could be inferred, and we don't know what was in the jurors' minds as they saw those buttons. But the point is that it could affect the outcome. It is an impermissible factor that causes the possibility that the jurors' verdict is based on something other than the evidence."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2006-05-785",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4c248d0c5593e03babd6a9a038208dbf64ae4cbfd9243e184c96d2d1537477a1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4c248d0c5593-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: Let's assume -- risk of what?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2006-05-785",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4c248d0c5593e03babd6a9a038208dbf64ae4cbfd9243e184c96d2d1537477a1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4c248d0c5593-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOUTER: Do you have to depend on there being a message? Isn't it enough if there is an influence that is conveyed?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2006-05-785",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4c248d0c5593e03babd6a9a038208dbf64ae4cbfd9243e184c96d2d1537477a1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4c248d0c5593-0002-0007",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 47,
        "start": 47
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "REBUTTAL ARGUMENT GREGORY A. OTT, ON BEHALF OF THE PETITIONER"
    },
    {
